----\n2545 |     pos_label : int, float, bool or str\n2546 |         If `pos_label` can be inferred, it will be returned.\n2547 | \n2548 |     Raises\n2549 |     ------\n2550 |     ValueError\n2551 |         In the case that `y_true` does not have label in {-1, 1} or {0, 1},\n2552 |         it will raise a `ValueError`.\n2553 |     \"\"\"\n2554 |     # ensure binary classification if pos_label is not specified\n2555 |     # classes.dtype.kind in ('O', 'U', 'S') is required to avoid\n2556 |     # triggering a FutureWarning by calling np.array_equal(a, b)\n2557 |     # when elements in the two arrays are not comparable.\n2558 |     if pos_label is None:\n2559 |         # Compute classes only if pos_label is not specified:\n2560 |         classes = np.unique(y_true)\n2561 |         if classes.dtype.kind in \"OUS\" or not (\n2562 |             np.array_equal(classes, [0, 1])\n2563 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [-1, 1])\n2564 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [0])\n2565 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [-1])\n2566 |             or np.array_equal(classes, [1])\n2567 |         ):\n2568 |             classes_repr = \", \".join([repr(c) for c in classes.tolist()])\n2569 |             raise ValueError(\n2570 |                 f\"y_true takes value in {{{classes_repr}}} and pos_label is not \"\n2571 |                 \"specified: either make y_true take value in {0, 1} or \"\n2572 |                 \"{-1, 1} or pass pos_label explicitly.\"\n2573 |             )\n2574 |         pos_label = 1\n2575 | \n2576 |     return pos_label\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me check the specific implementation mentioned in the issue:\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['sklearn/utils/_testing.py:assert_docstring_consistency']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/utils/_tes