mpression options if\n3799 |                compression mode is 'zip'.\n3800 | \n3801 |                Passing compression options as keys in dict is\n3802 |                supported for compression modes 'gzip', 'bz2', 'zstd', and 'zip'.\n3803 |         quoting : optional constant from csv module\n3804 |             Defaults to csv.QUOTE_MINIMAL. If you have set a `float_format`\n3805 |             then floats are converted to strings and thus csv.QUOTE_NONNUMERIC\n3806 |             will treat them as non-numeric.\n3807 |         quotechar : str, default '\\\"'\n3808 |             String of length 1. Character used to quote fields.\n3809 |         lineterminator : str, optional\n3810 |             The newline character or character sequence to use in the output\n3811 |             file. Defaults to `os.linesep`, which depends on the OS in which\n3812 |             this method is called ('\\\\n' for linux, '\\\\r\\\\n' for Windows, i.e.).\n3813 | \n3814 |             .. versionchanged:: 1.5.0\n3815 | \n3816 |                 Previously was line_terminator, changed for consistency with\n3817 |                 read_csv and the standard library 'csv' module.\n3818 | \n3819 |         chunksize : int or None\n3820 |             Rows to write at a time.\n3821 |         date_format : str, default None\n3822 |             Format string for datetime objects.\n3823 |         doublequote : bool, default True\n3824 |             Control quoting of `quotechar` inside a field.\n3825 |         escapechar : str, default None\n3826 |             String of length 1. Character used to escape `sep` and `quotechar`\n3827 |             when appropriate.\n3828 |         decimal : str, default '.'\n3829 |             Character recognized as decimal separator. E.g. use ',' for\n3830 |             European data.\n3831 |         errors : str, default 'strict'\n3832 |             Specifies how encoding and decoding errors are to be handled.\n3833 |             See the errors argument for :fun