309 |             start_i = i * self.chunksize\n310 |             end_i = min(start_i + self.chunksize, nrows)\n311 |             if start_i >= end_i:\n312 |                 break\n313 |             self._save_chunk(start_i, end_i)\n314 | \n315 |     def _save_chunk(self, start_i: int, end_i: int) -> None:\n316 |         # create the data for a chunk\n317 |         slicer = slice(start_i, end_i)\n318 |         df = self.obj.iloc[slicer]\n319 | \n320 |         res = df._get_values_for_csv(**self._number_format)\n321 |         data = list(res._iter_column_arrays())\n322 | \n323 |         ix = (\n324 |             self.data_index[slicer]._get_values_for_csv(**self._number_format)\n325 |             if self.nlevels != 0\n326 |             else np.empty(end_i - start_i)\n327 |         )\n328 |         libwriters.write_csv_rows(\n329 |             data,\n330 |             ix,\n331 |             self.nlevels,\n332 |             self.cols,\n333 |             self.writer,\n334 |         )\n```\n"}, {"content": "Based on my analysis, here are the relevant locations that need modification to add examples for the `float_format` parameter in the documentation:\n\n```\npandas/io/formats/csvs.py\nline: 180-188\nclass: CSVFormatter\nfunction: _number_format\n\npandas/io/formats/csvs.py\nline: 259-268\nclass: CSVFormatter\nfunction: save\n\npandas/io/formats/csvs.py\nline: 305-314\nclass: CSVFormatter\nfunction: _save_body\n\npandas/io/formats/csvs.py\nline: 315-319\nclass: CSVFormatter\nfunction: _save_chunk\n\npandas/core/generic.py\nline: 3727-3731\nclass: NDFrame\nfunction: to_csv\n```\n\nExplanation of why these locations are relevant:\n\n1. `pandas/io/formats/csvs.py:_number_format` - This is where the float_format setting is applied and stored. The dictionary that maps configuration options to their respective implementations is defined here.\n\n2. `pandas/io/formats/csvs.py:save` - This is where the actual CSV writing begins. The float format is applied during this stage thr